  "description": "RSCLIP is a vision-language foundation model for remote sensing, trained on 9.6M vision-language pairs generated without human annotation using InstructBLIP and remote sensing datasets. It uses a CLIP framework with a ViT-Base vision encoder and BERT-base text encoder, and demonstrates state-of-the-art performance on zero-shot classification, image-text retrieval, and semantic localization tasks.",
